<title>SWITZERLAND: Von Roll says 1996 net higher, no dividend.</title>
<headline>Von Roll says 1996 net higher, no dividend.</headline>
<dateline>GERLAFINGEN, Switzerland 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Group net			30.0		vs 26.7</p>
<p> Operating profit	     46.7		vs 47.7</p>
<p>Note - Von Roll Holding AG said it would not pay a dividend after posting an extraordinary loss at the holding level of 89 million Swiss francs. &quot;It is clear that we will therefore not pay a dividend,&quot; a spokesman told Reuters after the 1996 results were released in a statement.</p>
<p>The statement said the holding loss was due to charges for past and expected future costs from the steel business.</p>
<p>Von Roll's statement said the sale of its Swiss steel and aerial tram units last year, part of focusing on core engineering activities, had reduced figures for sales and orders.</p>
</text>
